          "filename": "Plaza de Toros de Ronda (6931270794).jpg",
          "caption": "The Plaza de Toros (\"bullring\") in Ronda, Málaga is one of the oldest operational bullrings in Spain. The arena has a diameter of 66 metres (217 ft), surrounded by a passage formed by two rings of stone. There are two layers of seating, each with five raised rows and 136 pillars that make up 68 arches. The Royal Box has a sloping roof covered in Arabic tiles.\n\nPlaza de Toros de Ronda. (2012, January 22). In Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia. Retrieved 19:18, April 14, 2012, from en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Plaza_de_Toros_de_Rond...",
